#Референс_Claude_Note_Memory_Patterns<[
Базис:
  Claude Note turns Claude Code sessions into durable notes through hooks, a file queue, a debounced worker, transcript synthesis, KnowledgePack JSON, note routing and MEMORY.md/Obsidian output.
  Work Graph already has stronger project-state contracts: WorkItem v1, Evidence Record v1, Worker Input/Output v1 and Project Memory v1.
  Therefore Claude Note is a reference for memory extraction mechanics, not a replacement for Work Graph memory or evidence source of truth.
Вектор:
  Adopt the extraction loop shape: observed agent events produce a bounded extraction job, the worker waits until the run is stable, reads structured run/transcript facts, synthesizes candidate memory, deduplicates against nearby records and writes human-readable memory artifacts.
  Adapt KnowledgePack into Project Memory v1: concepts, decisions, open questions, how-tos, highlights and task outcomes become typed MemoryRecord candidates with sourceWorkItem, evidenceIds, relatedTasks, relatedFiles, confidence and status.
  Keep note/vault output as readable projection: MEMORY.md or Obsidian-style notes can help humans and agents scan decisions, gotchas and how-tos, but canonical memory remains structured .bvc plus derived JSON export.
Цель:
  Work Graph gains an evidence-linked memory extraction loop that preserves useful session knowledge without dumping transcripts or letting provider-specific notes become project truth.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: claude-note-memory-patterns
  work.source: analyze-claude-note-memory-extractor-reference
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Паттерны_Взять<[
Базис:
  Claude Note has a compact architecture for turning ephemeral agent sessions into searchable human notes.
Вектор:
  Hooks/events: observe UserPromptSubmit, PostToolUse and Stop-like milestones as candidate extraction signals; in Work Graph these map to worker-run completion, evidence creation, verification result, human decision and blocker-resolution events.
  Queue/worker/debounce: use a small extraction queue with debounce or stabilization delay so memory is generated after a coherent unit of work, not after every tool call.
  Transcript/run reader: extract user intent, touched files, tools/commands, errors, changed artifacts and final outcome; prefer Worker Output and Evidence v1 first, with transcript/logs only as supporting artifacts.
  KnowledgePack shape: keep highlights, concepts, decisions, open questions, how-tos and note_ops as a useful synthesis envelope before normalizing into MemoryRecord v1.
  Note routing: route extracted items by project, domain, task, related files and memory type; support safe inbox/needs-review mode before direct updates.
  Dedup/semantic nearby notes: compare candidate records with existing active memory by type, related files/tasks, evidence ids and semantic similarity to update or supersede instead of duplicating.
  Human-readable output: maintain MEMORY.md or Obsidian-style sections for Decisions, Patterns, Gotchas, How-tos and Open Questions as a derived readable projection.
Цель:
  Adopt the operational loop and readability benefits while keeping Work Graph contracts responsible for durable state and traceability.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  reference.id: claude-note-patterns-to-adopt
  decision.id: claude-note-memory-patterns
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Маппинг_KnowledgePack_To_Project_Memory<[
Базис:
  Claude Note KnowledgePack is optimized for note synthesis, while Project Memory v1 is optimized for evidence-linked project context.
Вектор:
  highlights -> evidence-summary or architecture-fact candidates when they summarize verified work; each candidate must reference sourceWorkItem and evidenceIds.
  concepts -> architecture-fact, domain-fact or invariant records depending on whether the concept describes system structure, domain behavior or a rule future work must preserve.
  decisions -> decision records with basisLink/vectorLink/goalLink when available, evidenceIds for the supporting run/test/review and relatedTasks for follow-up impact.
  open_questions -> open-question records with status=draft or needs-review, relatedTasks and a next-action phrase in summary.
  howtos -> invariant, architecture-fact or domain-fact records only when the instruction is reusable and project-specific; generic tips stay out of project memory.
  task outcomes -> evidence-summary or decision records linked to the completed WorkItem, verification evidence and changed artifacts.
  note_ops -> memory writer operations: create candidate, update active record, append evidence id, mark needs-review, supersede stale record or emit derived human-readable note.
Цель:
  KnowledgePack remains a useful intermediate synthesis format, but every durable memory item becomes a typed MemoryRecord v1 with provenance.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: knowledgepack-memoryrecord-mapping
  decision.id: claude-note-memory-patterns
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Паттерны_Не_Брать_Или_Отложить<[
Базис:
  Claude Note intentionally starts from provider transcripts and personal notes, while Work Graph needs auditable project memory tied to work state.
Вектор:
  Do not store raw transcript dumps as memory records; transcripts and provider logs belong in evidence artifacts or external logs, summarized through Evidence v1.
  Do not make Claude-specific synthesis, Claude CLI session files or Claude-only hook names part of the core memory protocol; they are provider adapter details.
  Do not let unreviewed note mutation become source of truth; direct route mode can exist only after deterministic writer validation and conflict handling.
  Do not treat Obsidian vault, MEMORY.md or vector/qmd index as canonical memory storage; they are derived human/retrieval projections.
  Defer automatic preference extraction unless the user explicitly marks a durable project preference.
  Defer model fallback, rich web session UI, vault-wide semantic routing and line-budget pruning until the MVP writer and review loop are reliable.
Цель:
  Prevent a useful auto-note pattern from weakening evidence gates, provider neutrality or the Project Memory source-of-truth boundary.

Метки:
  atom.profile: prompt_rule
  rule.id: claude-note-patterns-deferred-or-rejected
  decision.id: claude-note-memory-patterns
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Точки_Запуска_Extraction<[
Базис:
  Memory extraction should run when Work Graph has enough stable evidence to produce durable knowledge.
Вектор:
  After worker run: create draft candidates from Worker Output, patch summary, touched files, tool/command summaries and run evidence; keep status=draft unless verification is already successful.
  After verification: promote or update candidates with verification evidence; decisions, invariants and evidence-summary records can become active when gates pass.
  After human decision: create decision, user-preference or open-question records only from explicit operator review, approval, rejection or instruction.
  After blocker resolution: convert blocker evidence into risk, gotcha, how-to or invariant records when the resolution is reusable; link both blocker and resolution evidence.
  After protocol/domain artifact ingestion: create domain-fact or architecture-fact candidates from StepAtomDraft/domain adapters, with file refs and work item links.
Цель:
  Memory writes are event-driven by Work Graph lifecycle moments, not by arbitrary chat length or hidden provider session boundaries.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: memory-extraction-trigger-points
  decision.id: claude-note-memory-patterns
  trace.status: verified
]>

#MVP_Recommendations<[
Базис:
  Project Memory v1 already defines fields and storage boundaries, but needs an extraction policy before implementation.
Вектор:
  MVP writer input: WorkItem snapshot, structured Evidence v1 records, Worker Output summary, changed/touched files, existing nearby MemoryRecords and optional transcript/log artifact refs.
  MVP synthesis output: MemoryCandidate pack with candidate id, type, summary, sourceWorkItem, evidenceIds, relatedFiles, relatedTasks, confidence, status, duplicateOf/supersedes and proposed human-readable section.
  MVP storage: write Project Memory .bvc atoms as canonical draft/active records and generate derived JSON plus optional MEMORY.md sections.
  MVP routing mode: start with inbox/needs-review for new decisions, invariants and user preferences; allow automatic active evidence-summary records only when linked verification evidence succeeded.
  MVP dedup: deterministic key by type/sourceWorkItem/evidenceIds plus fuzzy summary comparison against nearby active records; conflicts update status=needs-review instead of overwriting.
  MVP integration: feed memory updates into operator dashboard snapshot and future agent memorySlice; do not build an independent Claude Note-style vault UI first.
Цель:
  Build the smallest useful memory extractor around Work Graph evidence, then add richer semantic routing and human note views after the writer is trustworthy.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: claude-note-memory-mvp-scope
  work.source: analyze-claude-note-memory-extractor-reference
  trace.status: verified
]>
#Референс_Claude_Note_Memory_Patterns<[
Базис:
  Claude Note turns Claude Code sessions into project knowledge through hooks, a file queue, a debounced worker, transcript synthesis, KnowledgePack JSON and human-readable MEMORY/Obsidian notes.
  Work Graph already defines Project Memory v1 as durable records linked to WorkItems and Evidence v1, so Claude Note is a reference for extraction mechanics rather than a replacement memory model.
  The useful idea is not "save the chat"; it is "extract reviewable project knowledge from observed events after useful work has happened".
Вектор:
  Adopt hook/event capture, debounced background extraction, transcript/event reading, KnowledgePack-like intermediate structure, routing/dedup and human-readable memory output.
  Adapt KnowledgePack into Project Memory v1 records with sourceWorkItem, evidenceIds, relatedTasks and relatedFiles instead of treating notes or transcripts as authoritative state.
  Keep synthesis provider-neutral: Claude can be one extractor provider, but the memory writer contract must not depend on Claude-only sessions, prompts or vault layout.
Цель:
  Work Graph gains a memory extraction loop that converts completed work, verification and human decisions into compact Project Memory records without replaying raw transcripts.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: claude-note-memory-patterns
  work.source: analyze-claude-note-memory-extractor-reference
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Паттерны_Взять<[
Базис:
  Claude Note has a clear operational loop: hooks emit events, queue stores them durably, worker waits for quiet time, reader builds session facts, synthesizer emits structured knowledge, router writes notes.
Вектор:
  Hooks/events: capture meaningful lifecycle events such as prompt submitted, tool used, worker finished, verification completed, human decision recorded and blocker resolved.
  Queue/worker/debounce: use a small durable extraction queue and per-session/per-task state so memory extraction runs after a stable pause, not while a worker is still changing files.
  Transcript/event reader: read bounded session facts such as user asks, tools used, files touched, commands run, errors and produced artifacts; do not pass an unbounded transcript directly to memory.
  KnowledgePack shape: keep an intermediate extraction object with highlights, concepts, decisions, open questions, howtos/task outcomes and proposed memory operations.
  Note routing: route proposed records by project, domain, work item, file and memory type; support safe modes such as log-only or inbox/needs-review before direct route.
  Dedup and semantic nearby notes: compare against existing memory records and nearby notes before creating new records; update/supersede when a fact already exists.
  Human-readable output: keep MEMORY.md or Obsidian-style projections as derived review surfaces for humans and agents that need a compact context file.
Цель:
  Preserve Claude Note's practical extraction loop while keeping Work Graph memory typed, auditable and source-linked.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  reference.id: claude-note-patterns-to-adopt
  decision.id: claude-note-memory-patterns
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Паттерны_Адаптировать<[
Базис:
  Claude Note's KnowledgePack is close to a useful extraction DTO, but Work Graph needs stronger links to WorkItem state and Evidence v1.
Вектор:
  highlights map to evidence-summary or task outcome records only when tied to sourceWorkItem and evidenceIds.
  concepts map to architecture-fact, domain-fact or invariant records based on whether they describe system structure, domain behavior or a rule that must persist.
  decisions map to decision records with basisLink/vectorLink/goalLink when they come from a protocol/task BVC, plus evidenceIds for verification or manual-review evidence.
  open_questions map to open-question records with relatedTasks and status=draft or needs-review; they can seed follow-up WorkItems but do not automatically become task state.
  howtos map to invariant or architecture-fact records only after successful command/test/manual evidence; otherwise they remain needs-review notes.
  note_ops map to memory writer operations: create record, update record, supersede/retire record or route to review inbox.
Цель:
  KnowledgePack becomes a staging format for Project Memory v1 writes, not the canonical memory store.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: knowledgepack-to-memory-record-v1
  protocol.id: project-memory-v1
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Паттерны_Не_Брать_Или_Отложить<[
Базис:
  Claude Note optimizes for personal note capture from Claude Code sessions, while Work Graph must preserve provider-neutral project state and evidence gates.
Вектор:
  Do not store full transcript dumps as memory; transcripts and provider logs are evidence artifacts or debugging material, not MemoryRecord summaries.
  Do not make Claude-only synthesis the memory architecture; extractor providers must consume neutral event/evidence inputs and emit the same staging schema.
  Do not allow unreviewed note mutation to become source of truth; direct writes can create draft/needs-review records unless backed by successful evidence or explicit human decision.
  Defer Obsidian vault routing, qmd/vector search, model fallback UI, tray/web sessions UI and MEMORY.md truncation policy until Project Memory writer/export paths exist.
  Defer automatic user-preference extraction; Project Memory v1 requires explicit confirmation for durable user-preference records.
Цель:
  Avoid turning Project Memory into a chat archive, provider feature clone or uncontrolled notes vault.

